course: dictionary
lesson: 6286
title: Monument: a word that remembers
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A monument is a statue, building or stone made to remember a famous person or event. Look at the context: «Berdiansk has a monument to the goby, the Goby Breadwinner, that fed people in hard years.» The clue is that the monument is made to remember a small fish that helped people survive.
explain: Monument can also mean an old building or place that is important in history, as in «an ancient monument». The word ancient is a clue: it tells you the monument is very old. Ask yourself, what would fit here? A stone circle or an old castle could be an ancient monument.
explain: A monument can also be a great example of something, as in «a monument to hard work». There is no statue here. Try your meaning in the sentence: if the person is a clear, big example of hard work, it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Climbing on statues, monuments and museum displays leads to falls on hard floors and damage that cannot be undone.» The sentence warns you not to climb on monuments, so you can tell they are valuable and must be kept safe. Context can teach you a lot even when the word is new.
fact: A monument is something made to remember a person or an event.
fact: «Monument» means a statue, building or stone made to remember something.
fact: An ancient monument is an old building or place that is important in history.
fact: A war memorial is a kind of monument that remembers people who died in war.
fact: Monument can also mean a great example of something, as in «a monument to hard work».
exercise: In «a monument to hard work», what does monument mean? | A stone statue in a park | A very old castle | A school trip to a museum | *A great example of hard work
exercise: «Climbing on statues, monuments and museum displays leads to falls.» What does the sentence warn you not to do? | Take photos of the sea | Visit museum displays with a teacher | Read history books | *Climb on statues and monuments
exercise: «The ancient monument stood on the hill.» Find and copy one word that means very old. | monument | *ancient | stood | hill
test: On 11 November, people remember those who died in war. What is a war memorial? | A kind of rain | A small fish | A school dinner | *A monument that remembers people who died in war
test: Why was the Goby Breadwinner monument made? | To sell fish in a shop | To mark a football pitch | To show a king's ship | *To remember a small fish that fed people in hard years
exam: Which phrase uses monument to mean a great example of something? | *A monument to hard work | A statue in the town square | A war memorial on 11 November | An ancient monument on the hill
